WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.173 --> 00:00:02.113
(hypnotic music)

00:00:02.113 --> 00:00:05.946
- [Narrator] This is
Pierre, a hooded vulture.

00:00:08.387 --> 00:00:10.369
Native to Sub-Saharan Africa,

00:00:10.369 --> 00:00:13.389
hooded vultures are critically endangered.

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:15.917
They are the smallest of African vultures,

00:00:15.917 --> 00:00:19.160
only slightly larger than a crow.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.461
They are scavengers.

00:00:20.461 --> 00:00:22.112
And because of their small size,

00:00:22.112 --> 00:00:24.077
they end up waiting by carcasses

00:00:24.077 --> 00:00:27.981
and eating the scraps left
behind by bigger birds.

00:00:27.981 --> 00:00:30.424
Adults have white
feathers behind the neck,

00:00:30.424 --> 00:00:33.208
which forms a hood over its head.

00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:35.672
They live in forest
clearings where it rains,

00:00:35.672 --> 00:00:38.765
coastal marshes, and lagoons.

00:00:38.765 --> 00:00:40.907
Hooded vultures are unafraid of humans

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.491
and can be found in villages and towns,

00:00:43.491 --> 00:00:47.213
often referred to as garbage
collectors by locals.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.560
Due to a combination
of hunting, poisoning,

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.291
and habitat degradation, their population

00:00:52.291 --> 00:00:56.845
over the last three generations
has declined over 80%.

00:00:56.845 --> 00:00:59.095
This is the hooded vulture.

